# Author lock

Nathan clicking **Save** / **Save all** / Ctrl+S in Roster, the card editor, the Script editor, or the HTML board stamps `author_lock` on that text. Ledger: `data/author-locks.json`. Flags also live on the card in `data/content-board.json` and on each row in `data/player-copy.json`.

## Every message

Read `data/author-locks.json` (and the flags on the board / script). Treat locked fields as finished writing.

## Do not

- Do not rewrite locked `name`, `ability`, `explainer`, `flow`, `notes`, `ops`, numbers, rarity, tier, count, priority, or locked script `text`.
- Do not "clean up", Title Case, keyword-paint, shorten, or restyle locked copy in JSON or by changing the live fallback that players actually see.
- Do not strip `author_lock`, `locked_fields`, or `locked_at`.

## If chat asks to change locked text

1. Stop. Do not edit it in that turn.
2. Name the locked keys (card id + fields, or script key + current line).
3. Ask whether this message is an override.
4. Change them only after he clearly says yes to those named keys.

His Save in the editor updates locked text. That is allowed. Chat is not, unless he overrides.

`status` (`todo` / `live` / `hold`) is not locked. You may still implement Flow and set `live` after shipping behavior, without rewriting locked player sentences.
